    "rationaleRequired": true,
    "rationale": "The corrected selection contains 15 pro moves and 12 con moves because the retained source contains additional independently load-bearing pro claims rather than because of a counting threshold. In science and the partnership claim, Sacks's DNA-reconsideration analogy is distinct from his motion-level compatible-roles claim, while Dawkins supplies one retained purpose-domain challenge. In literal, symbolic, and scientific interpretation, Sacks separately offers the Red Sea mechanism, the Adam-and-Eve parable reason, and the general scientific-incompatibility rule, while Dawkins supplies the broader literalism test and the classification-rule challenge. In Abraham and Isaac, Sacks separately gives the anti-sacrifice interpretation, the culturally situated explanation of the ordeal's form, and the later interpretive concession, while Dawkins gives the direct-instruction objection and the child-abuse rejoinder. In community and a post-religious future, Dawkins has four distinct load-bearing moves—the measurement question, the community-mechanism concession, the proposed secular substitute, and the historical-trend reply—while Sacks has the Putnam evidence, the narrow religious-and-secular-causes clarification, and the persistence challenge. In the closing section, Sacks's shared-scientific-integrity claim and his separate transcendence-for-dignity claim both remain load-bearing, while Dawkins's single closing move combines common moral ground with the supernatural divide. These source-grounded asymmetries should not be erased by merging distinct claims or importing excluded conversation."
